NEARS-1573 — a store-list NETWORK FAILURE renders the AC6 "nothing open nearby" message
Code-derived (not device-reproduced: could not cut the app's API without a rebuild; see QA notes).

UserApp/lib/features/store/controllers/store_controller.dart, getStoreList():
    if (storeModel == null && offset == 1 && emptyOnClientFailure && _storeModel == null) {
      // NEARS-603/671: a null client model = network failure ...
      _storeModel = StoreModel(stores: <Store>[], totalSize: 0, offset: 1);
      _storeLoadFailed = true;
      update();
    }

UserApp/lib/features/home/controllers/home_controller.dart:211 loads the module-home store list with
    emptyOnClientFailure: true

Consequence for the new gate:
    hasOpenStoreNearby -> activeStoresIncludingClosed(<empty list>) -> [] (non-null)
                       -> [].any(...) -> FALSE
    grocery_home_screen.dart: `if (storeController.hasOpenStoreNearby == false) return _NothingOpenNearbyView();`
=> On a transient store-list network failure the whole grocery module body is replaced with
   "Service not available in this area / Please change your delivery location", steering the customer
   to change their address for what is a connectivity error.

The distinguishing flag already exists and is already consumed elsewhere on the SAME screen:
   StoreController.storeLoadFailed -> home_screen.dart:485 passes it to the all-stores ItemView
   (NEARS-603 / NEARS-671 precedent). The new gate does not read it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LIVE REPRO (device-proven, emulator-5554)

Harness: scripts/qa-tools/qa_fail_proxy.py serve --run-key NEARS-1573 --target http://127.0.0.1:8000
         (resolved port 24318); app rebuilt with --dart-define=API_HOST=10.0.2.2:24318.
         `pm clear com.izzes.nears` first, so there is no local store cache (the _storeModel == null guard).
Fault ON:  qa_fail_proxy.py fail --run-key NEARS-1573 --slug all --status 500

Proxy access log (only these were injected; everything else passed through 200):
  *** INJECTED 500 for /api/v1/home/all
  *** INJECTED 500 for /api/v1/stores/get-stores/all?store_type=all&offset=1&limit=12
  "GET /api/v1/categories HTTP/1.1" 200
  "GET /api/v1/items/popular?... HTTP/1.1" 200
  "GET /api/v1/flash-sales HTTP/1.1" 200
  "GET /api/v1/banners HTTP/1.1" 200

App log (adb logcat -s flutter):
  [NET]  endpoint=/api/v1/stores/get-stores/all http_status=500
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/stores/get-stores/all http_status=500 type=ApiFailure msg="api request failed"
  [NET]  endpoint=/api/v1/home/all http_status=500
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/home/all http_status=500 type=ApiFailure msg="unhandled api response"

OBSERVED on the Grocery home: the entire module body is
  "Service not available in this area"
  "Please change your delivery location to access our services"
  [Change Location]
No error/retry affordance anywhere. Categories and items had loaded fine (200).

Fault OFF (qa_fail_proxy.py clear --run-key NEARS-1573), same screen re-entered:
  Available Near You renders 6 tiles — 0.36 / 0.39 / 0.91 / 1.19 / 3.84 / 4.49 KM FROM YOU,
  CLOSES 21:00 / 22:00 / 23:00 — plus Trending Nearby.
=> the empty state was caused by the store-list failure, not by the data.

Note on scope: the proxy matches the trailing path segment, so `--slug all` also hit /api/v1/home/all.
The gate under test reads ONLY storeModel (set by /stores/get-stores/all), so the store-list 500 is
the operative cause; /home/all failing cannot populate storeModel with an empty list.
